# Declares intent: raw test artifacts are referenced by path in reports, while
# execution summaries, curated reports and structured JSON/Markdown stay readable.
# See docs/artifact-strategy.md and .claude/rules/core/token-discipline.md.
#
# NOTE: Claude Code does not currently enforce .claudeignore for tool reads
# (verified 2026-09-05: a file under evidence/ was still readable via the Read
# tool). This file documents the policy; the enforced boundary is the raw-artifact
# permissions denylist in .claude/settings.json, not a blanket evidence/ deny.
evidence/.mcp-out/
**/evidence/.mcp-out/
**/evidence/**/*.png
**/evidence/**/*.jpg
**/evidence/**/*.jpeg
**/evidence/**/*.gif
**/evidence/**/*.webp
**/evidence/**/*.bmp
**/evidence/**/*.webm
**/evidence/**/*.mp4
**/evidence/**/*.mov
**/evidence/**/*.zip
**/evidence/**/*.har

# Secrets — defense in depth alongside .gitignore and the permissions denylist
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installer backups and node_modules never need to be in context
*.bak-*
node_modules/
